     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi, I&#39;m working on a shiny app to help some human coders do some coding of images. I have some radio buttons and a checkbox group. After I have the user click submit, I&#39;d like the radio buttons to be reset. Unfortunately, it seems that only the first set of radio buttons (raceId) resets after submit is clicked, genderId and practice area do not.  Seems like something subtle going on here with reactivity, but it&#39;s beyond me. Any help would be appreciated</div><div><br></div><div>    observeEvent(input$Submit,{</div><div>      updateRadioButtons(session=session,</div><div>                         inputId = &quot;raceId&quot;,</div><div>                         choices=list(&quot;White&quot;,</div><div>                                      &quot;Black&quot;,</div><div>                                      &quot;Unidentified&quot;),</div><div>                         selected=character(0))</div><div><br></div><div>      updateRadioButtons(session=session,</div><div>                         inputId = &quot;genderId&quot;,</div><div>                         choices=list(&quot;Male&quot;,</div><div>                                      &quot;Female&quot;,</div><div>                                      &quot;Unidentified&quot;),</div><div>                         selected=character(0))</div><div><br></div><div>      updateCheckboxGroupInput(session = session,</div><div>                               inputId = &quot;practiceArea&quot;,</div><div>                               selected=NULL)</div><div><br></div><div>    })#end observe event</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
